sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant S as TCP Socket Buffer<br/>(kernel receive buffer)
    participant CT as Controller
    participant W as Worker
    participant V as Volume

    C->>S: HTTP PUT /objects/:id<br/>headers (object metadata, Content-Length) + body bytes
    Note over C,S: Backpressure via TCP flow control: as the receive buffer fills,<br/>the advertised window (rwnd) shrinks and the client's sends slow or stall

    CT->>S: async non-blocking read (network I/O)
    S-->>CT: HTTP headers + complete object metadata
    Note over CT: Persist object metadata (state = UPLOADING)<br/>Allocate object_id

    loop for each chunk until Content-Length bytes are consumed
        CT->>S: async read of exactly 1 chunk (e.g. 8 MiB) into a bounded buffer
        S-->>CT: chunk bytes (frees buffer space, rwnd reopens)
        CT-)W: async HTTP PUT /chunks (network I/O)<br/>object_id, chunk_id, seq_no, length, checksum + chunk data
        activate W
        W-)V: async write (disk I/O): chunk data
        V--)W: write completion (after fsync)
        Note over W: Record chunk info locally<br/>chunk_id → volume, offset, length, checksum
        W--)CT: 201 ACK: chunk_id, seq_no, location, checksum
        deactivate W
        Note over CT: Persist chunk map entry<br/>seq_no → worker, volume, offset<br/>Release chunk buffer, then read next chunk
    end

    Note over CT: All chunks ACKed → commit object manifest (state = COMPLETE)
    CT->>S: write HTTP response
    S-->>C: 201 Created (object_id, ETag)
